{
  "layout": "stack",
  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "status",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "value": "## GitHub"
        },
        {
          "type": "auth_status",
          "bind": "GET /api/apps/git/status",
          "logout_action": {
            "call": "POST /api/apps/git/logout"
          },
          "loading_text": "Checking GitHub login…",
          "logged_in_text": "Signed in as **{username}**",
          "logged_out_text": "Not signed in yet — use either option below. Both do the same thing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "signed-in-detail",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "auth_status",
          "bind": "GET /api/apps/git/status",
          "loading_text": "",
          "logged_in_text": "Credential: `{token_masked}` · {token_kind}\n\nCommits authored as **{git_user_name}** &lt;{git_user_email}&gt;\n\nAccess: {scopes_text}",
          "logged_out_text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sign-in",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "hide_when_logged_in": true,
          "value": "### Option 1 — Sign in with GitHub\nEasiest. Click below, then enter the one-time code at [github.com/login/device](https://github.com/login/device). Your git commit name and email are filled in for you.\n\nGrants access to your repositories. If you also need to publish container images or manage an organisation's runners, use Option 2 instead — that access can only come from a token."
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "hide_when_logged_in": true,
          "label": "Sign in with GitHub",
          "action": {
            "call": "POST /api/apps/git/device/start",
            "poll": {
              "call": "POST /api/apps/git/device/poll",
              "interval_ms": 3000,
              "timeout_ms": 900000,
              "done_field": "status",
              "done_values": [
                "success",
                "expired_token",
                "access_denied",
                "error"
              ],
              "pending_text": "Waiting for authorization on [github.com/login/device](https://github.com/login/device)…",
              "timeout_text": "Timed out — click Sign in with GitHub again."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "token",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "hide_when_logged_in": true,
          "value": "### Option 2 — Paste a token\nUse this when you need more than repository access. Create one at [github.com/settings/tokens](https://github.com/settings/tokens) with the scopes you need (`write:packages` to publish images, `admin:org` to manage runners). Your git commit name and email are filled in for you here too."
        },
        {
          "type": "form",
          "id": "token_signin",
          "hide_when_logged_in": true,
          "submit": {
            "call": "POST /api/apps/git/settings"
          },
          "submit_label": "Sign in with token",
          "fields": [
            {
              "key": "github_token",
              "label": "Personal access token",
              "input": "password",
              "placeholder": "ghp_… / github_pat_…"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "collapsible",
          "title": "Replace token",
          "collapsed": true,
          "widgets": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "value": "Paste a new token to replace the stored one — useful when you need extra access, e.g. publishing container images. Stored encrypted and re-applied on every restart."
            },
            {
              "type": "form",
              "id": "token_replace",
              "submit": {
                "call": "POST /api/apps/git/settings"
              },
              "submit_label": "Save token",
              "fields": [
                {
                  "key": "github_token",
                  "label": "Personal access token",
                  "input": "password",
                  "placeholder": "ghp_… / github_pat_…"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "advanced",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "collapsible",
          "title": "Advanced",
          "collapsed": true,
          "widgets": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "value": "Override the git commit identity, or point the Sign in button at your own GitHub OAuth App. Both are optional — signing in fills the identity in for you."
            },
            {
              "type": "form",
              "id": "advanced_settings",
              "submit": {
                "call": "POST /api/apps/git/settings"
              },
              "submit_label": "Save",
              "fields": [
                {
                  "key": "git_user_name",
                  "label": "Git user.name",
                  "input": "text",
                  "placeholder": "Jane Doe"
                },
                {
                  "key": "git_user_email",
                  "label": "Git user.email",
                  "input": "text",
                  "placeholder": "jane@example.com"
                },
                {
                  "key": "oauth_client_id",
                  "label": "OAuth App client_id",
                  "input": "text",
                  "placeholder": "Ov23liWR67ZgY2P6fYKh (default, already configured)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
